Data note: figures are ecosystem-wide—not market share for the three brands studied. Values and volumes are reported from CBN
annual-report data and published coverage.
03
METHODOLOGY & SCOPE
Research design
Exploratory secondary research using public company websites, product pages, regulator material and published
reporting. The analysis compares visible propositions and market context; it does not estimate market share or claim
customer sentiment without primary evidence.
Research questions
1
What products, services
and use cases does each
competitor emphasise?
2
Which audiences and
customer problems
appear central to each
proposition?
3
How does each brand
frame value, trust,
convenience and
growth?
4
Where do the brands
overlap—and where
could differentiation be
created?
Analytical lenses
COMPETITIVE INTELLIGENCE
Product breadth, merchant/agent
infrastructure, visible
differentiators and overlap.
MARKET RESEARCH
Customer segments, needs, usage
contexts, friction points and unmet
needs inferred from market
structure and public messaging.
These remain hypotheses.
POSITIONING
Brand promise, emphasis,
audience, benefit framing and
possible white-space
opportunities.
LIMITATIONS
Company pages are promotional. Metrics can vary by definition and date. Public product features do not reveal
adoption, satisfaction or retention. No primary interviews, surveys, usability tests or transaction-level dataset were
collected for this report.

