Independent desk research4
04
COMPETITIVE INTELLIGENCE
MONIEPOINT
Business growth & operations
OBSERVED
PROPOSITION
An integrated financial and business platform with business banking, POS acceptance,
expense cards, working capital, savings and business management tools such as
Moniebook.
AUDIENCE EMPHASIS
Merchants, SMEs and businesses, extending into personal banking and broader financial
services.
MESSAGING CUES
Business growth, operational convenience, payment reliability, financial tools and
managing activity in one ecosystem.
STRENGTHS INDICATED
Business-focused breadth; linking payment acceptance to banking, credit and
operations; merchant-centric language; clear POS and management use cases.
TENSION TO
INVESTIGATE
Broad product breadth may create complexity. Opportunity: make integrated value easier
to understand by business size and stage.
OPAY
Everyday financial utility
OBSERVED
PROPOSITION
A broad financial-services platform combining transfers, bill payments, debit cards,
savings, merchant services and agent/POS solutions.
AUDIENCE EMPHASIS
Consumers seeking everyday payment utility, plus merchants and agents using financial
services to serve communities.
MESSAGING CUES
Convenience, affordability, speed, incentives, security, inclusion and “one app” utility.
STRENGTHS INDICATED
Breadth of everyday services; rewards/pricing cues; merchant and agent tools; a
utility-led narrative across personal and business use.
TENSION TO
INVESTIGATE
Broad all-in-one positioning may be difficult to distinguish. A clearer benefit hierarchy for
key segments could make the promise more memorable.
PALMPAY
Consumer value & rewards
OBSERVED
PROPOSITION
A consumer-focused financial app combining transfers, savings, rewards, bills, cards and
credit, with a parallel merchant/POS proposition.
AUDIENCE EMPHASIS
Everyday consumers seeking low-friction transactions, rewards and savings, alongside
merchants seeking payment acceptance.
MESSAGING CUES
Rewards, free transfers, savings returns, ease, accessibility, financial progress and
everyday value.
STRENGTHS INDICATED
Consumer-value framing; visible reward cues; savings/payment utility; extending into
merchant services.
TENSION TO
INVESTIGATE
Incentives can be copied. Durable differentiation may rely on experience, trust, relevance
and service quality.

