Independent desk research8
09
CONCLUSION
Nigeria’s fintech competition is moving beyond access toward which platform becomes most useful—and
trusted—in a customer’s everyday financial life or business operation. Moniepoint, OPay and PalmPay each offer
broad service ecosystems, but their public messaging creates different emphasis: merchant operations, broad
financial utility and consumer value respectively.
As product capabilities converge, durable advantage is likely to come from a clearer customer promise, superior
experience in a specific use case, stronger trust and service recovery, and consistent evidence that the brand
delivers. The opportunity is not simply to add another feature. It is to make a customer’s reason for choosing—and
staying with—a platform unmistakably clear.
THE STRATEGIC QUESTION
What customer problem can a fintech solve so consistently and credibly
that the customer stops comparing features and begins preferring the
brand?
